{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And the days of Israel drew near to die.</b> Whoever 'drawing near to die' is said of did not reach the days of his fathers (Isaac lived 180, and Jacob 147; of David 'drawing near' is said — his father lived 80 years and he lived 70)." "<b>And he called his son, to Joseph.</b> To the one who had the power in his hand to do it." "<b>Put now your hand.</b> And swear." "<b>Kindness and truth.</b> Kindness done with the dead is kindness of truth, for one does not look forward to payment of recompense." "<b>Bury me not, I pray, in Egypt.</b> In the end its dust will become lice, and they will crawl beneath my body, and the dead outside the Land live only in pain of the rolling of the passages, and that the Egyptians not make me an idolatry."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:53.843289842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}